NNAAMMEE
     nnffssdduummppssttaattee — display NFSv4 open/lock state

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     nnffssdduummppssttaattee [--oo] [--ll _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     nnffssdduummppssttaattee displays open/lock state for the NFSv4 client and server in
     the experimental nfs subsystem.

     The options are as follows:

     --oo      Displays a summary of Clients for NFSv4. Each line lists a Client
             with the ClientID being the last field of the line.

             The following are the client flag values displayed:
               NC    Needs Confirmation
               CB    Callbacks are enabled
               GSS   Using RPCSEC_GSS
               REV   Administratively Revoked, via nfsrevoke(8)

     --ll _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e
             Displays a list of all NFSv4 Opens and Locks on the file speci‐
             fied by the _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e.  The ClientID is the last field of each
             line.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     nfsv4(4), nfsrevoke(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The nnffssdduummppssttaattee utility was introduced with the NFSv4 experimental sub‐
     system in 2009.

